13	/**
14	 * GAME_CONFIG handler — apply a game server's customization (variant + settings).
15	 *
16	 * `worker/index.ts` owns the job loop and its `handlers` map; wire this in there:
17	 *   GAME_CONFIG: gameConfigApply,
18	 *
19	 * Ownership + validation happen at enqueue time (lib/actions-game-config.ts), so
20	 * this handler trusts `Server.gameVariant` / `Server.gameConfig`.
21	 *
22	 * TWO PATHS:
23	 *  - DEFAULT (simulation): records an "applied" marker on `Server.gameConfig` and
24	 *    notifies the user. No SSH, no VM mutation. This runs under SANDBOX and, in
25	 *    production, for any family not yet verified (see below).
26	 *
27	 *  - REAL: actually pushes the settings to the live game server over SSH. Runs
28	 *    per-family (see `REAL_APPLY_FAMILIES`) rather than one blanket switch — a
29	 *    family's real path is deliberately non-destructive (read-modify-write for
30	 *    key=value files, or — for images like Palworld's that regenerate their
31	 *    config from env vars on every boot — a full container recreation with
32	 *    rollback on failure; never clobbers a config it can't find/parse) and
33	 *    fully wrapped in try/catch so a failure notifies the user but never
34	 *    crashes the worker. `ENABLE_REAL_GAMECFG=1` additionally force-enables
35	 *    every family at once, for whenever the rest have been confirmed too.
36	 *
37	 * Enable a family's real path only once its config paths / service names / apply
38	 * function have been confirmed for the actual game-server image — see
39	 * `REAL_APPLY_FAMILIES`'s own comment for what "confirmed" means in practice.
40	 */
