46	/**
47	 * Families whose real-apply path has been individually built AND verified
48	 * against the actual production image/container, so it's safe to run even
49	 * while `ENABLE_REAL_GAMECFG` stays off for everyone else.
50	 *
51	 * "verified" here means: confirmed live, end-to-end, against a real running
52	 * container — not just "the code looks right". `palworld` was added
53	 * 2026-09-05 after the previous version of `applyPalworld` was found to
54	 * silently regenerate-then-lose its own writes (see that function's comment);
55	 * the replacement was verified by actually recreating a live container with
56	 * an updated setting and reading the resulting config back off disk.
57	 *
58	 * `minecraft` added 2026-09-06: verified against a real throwaway server on
59	 * node-2 (provisioned, applied `difficulty` + `online-mode` via
60	 * `applyRealConfig` directly, read `/opt/mc/server.properties` back off disk
61	 * and confirmed both values, then destroyed the VM). The path-detection
62	 * TODO on `applyMinecraft` is resolved for the current image: the host-side
63	 * bind mount (`/opt/mc` -> `/data`) puts server.properties somewhere
64	 * `remoteLocate`'s `find` over /opt already reaches. One real, non-blocking
65	 * gap found: `mcrcon` is not installed on the image, so today every setting
66	 * falls back to "restart to apply" — correctly reported as such, never
67	 * silently claimed live — rather than the live-RCON push `tryMinecraftRcon`
68	 * would otherwise attempt for difficulty/whitelist/etc.
69	 */
70	const REAL_APPLY_FAMILIES = new Set<string>(["palworld", "minecraft"]);
